3. LIMITED HOSTED USE

Free personal play and employee-facilitated internal team-improvement workshops at one organization are permitted through the authorized hosted Slice of Flow service, subject to the separately approved and published Slice of Flow Terms of Use and applicable law. Ordinary employee salaries and internal training costs do not alone make such internal use a separately licensed external offering.

Normal browser loading, caching and execution needed to use that authorized service are permitted. This permission is not a license to run a mirror or your own hosted copy, distribute source or an offline edition, white-label the product, or grant rights to others. Sending someone a link to the authorized service does not grant a sublicense; that person’s use is governed by the applicable terms or other valid rights.

This section will operate only with an approved, published hosted-use policy. The draft does not establish that any current visitor has accepted new restrictions or that permission validly received previously has ended.

4. EXTERNAL FACILITATION AND COMMERCIAL USE

Jeff Bourke’s express written authorization is required for external client, public, community, nonprofit, school or multi-organization facilitation, whether paid or unpaid. An outside coach or consultant facilitating for a client falls within this requirement even when participants are not charged or no separate game fee appears on an invoice.

Paid external training, consulting, conference, membership, subscription, certification or other external service bundles incorporating Slice of Flow require the appropriate written authorization. Ordinary employee-led internal use remains covered by Section 3; salaries and internal training costs alone do not trigger this requirement. A commercial facilitation authorization does not also authorize resale, rehosting, source distribution, offline editions, sublicensing, white-labeling, or distribution of protected course/template/facilitator materials. Those activities require their own express grant.

Written permission must identify the licensee and the authorized activity, audience, facilitators, materials, duration and any compensation. Only the stated rights are granted. Nothing in this notice transfers Jeff Bourke’s ownership. These requirements apply only to the extent supported by his actual rights or an enforceable agreement and remain subject to Section 6.

5. RESULTS, PRINTING AND ATTRIBUTION

During permitted hosted use, the service’s provided export and print functions may be used to obtain session summaries and debrief sheets. An unaltered results summary may be shared publicly or within a team, and reasonable debrief copies may be supplied to participants in an authorized workshop. Existing Slice of Flow and Jeff Bourke attribution on supplied materials must be retained where the applicable rights or agreement require it.

These permissions do not authorize selling supplied debrief sheets, repackaging protected materials into a commercial course or facilitator kit, removing attribution to imply your authorship, or representing Jeff Bourke as an endorser. Numerical results and facts are not claimed as Jeff Bourke’s copyrighted expression. Users retain any rights they have in their own original notes; independently reporting factual outcomes is not prohibited.

